  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued October 31 at 2:57AM MST until October 31 at 12:15PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Gila County in east central Arizona...

* WHEN...Until 1215 PM MST Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of Tonto Creek and flood-prone locations is
imminent or occurring. Tonto Creek continues to rise due to excess
runoff from earlier rainfall. Low-water crossings are inundated
with water and may not be passable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 248 AM MST, a streamflow gauge on Tonto Creek north of Tonto
Basin rose above action stage, with a stage height of 4.73 feet
at 215 AM MST. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly
along Tonto Creek in the warned area. Please use the Tonto Creek
Bridge for all travel across the creek. Bar X Crossing, and any
other low water crossings, will likely become impassable.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Tonto Basin.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
